# Git & Pull Requests (`ethereumjs/protocols`)

## Remote Git Discipline

Unless the human **explicitly** asks in the current message, do **not**:
- `git commit`
- `git push` (or force-push)
- `gh pr create` / open or merge pull requests
- switch branches (`git checkout` / `git switch`)

**Commit alone is not permission to push.** If the human asks to "commit", stop after `git commit` succeeds unless the same message also asks to push or open a PR.

## Multi-Root Workspace Execution

When running `git` or `gh` commands for this repository in a multi-root Cursor workspace:
1. Always set `working_directory: "/Users/holgerd/DEV/EthereumJS/protocols"`.
2. Use `required_permissions: ["all"]` when needed for signing / GitHub CLI access, and run signed git operations (`commit`, `push`, `pull`, `gh pr create`) **one shell command at a time** (sequentially, never in parallel) so Touch ID / SSH signing prompts do not collide.

## Pull Request Workflow

All changes to `main` flow through Pull Requests:
- Use concise, descriptive commit messages and PR titles (`ETHY/0 DevP2P protocol specification`, etc.).
- Mirror the PR title themes as `##` sections in the PR body explaining the protocol additions or refinements.
